{"name":"Blissful Meditation","hex":"#d5daee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blissful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extremely happy; full of joy; experiencing, indicating, causing, or characterized by bliss.","Blessed; glorified."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blissful"},{"term":"meditation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A devotional exercise of, or leading to, contemplation.","Any of various types of achieving more or less altered states of consciousness, such as vacancy of mind or prolonged contemplation on a single sensation or thought, through relaxed or focused mental and physical activity generally of a nonstrenuous and non–substance-induced nature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meditation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blissful","blocks":[{"text":"Blissful is the second album by drummer Hamid Drake and his group Bindu. It was recorded on July 12 and 13, 2007, at Soma Electronic Music Studios in Chicago, Illinois, and was issued on CD in 2008 by Rogueart. On the album, Drake is joined by vocalist Dee Alexander, guitarists Joe Morris and Jeff Parker, and double bassists Josh Abrams and William Parker. Lyrics were written by the 18th-century poet Ramprasad Sen, and were excerpted from Mother of the Universe: Visions of the Goddess and Tantric Hymns of Enlightenment by Lex Hixon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Hamid_Drake_Blissful.jpg/330px-Hamid_Drake_Blissful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blissful","wikidata":"Q125820751"},{"title":"Meditation","blocks":[{"text":"Meditation is a practice in which an individual uses a technique or combination of techniques to train attention and awareness and detach from \"discursive, ruminating thought\", achieving a mentally clear and emotionally calm and stable state, while not intending to analyze the effects, to judge its outcomes, or to create any expectation with regard to the process."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meditation","wikidata":"Q108458"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Swami_Vivekananda_1896.jpg/120px-Swami_Vivekananda_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Swami_Vivekananda_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Swami_Vivekananda_1896.jpg/120px-Swami_Vivekananda_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwami_Vivekananda_1896.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Hsuan_Hua_Hong_Kong_1.jpeg/330px-Hsuan_Hua_Hong_Kong_1.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Hsuan_Hua_Hong_Kong_1.jpeg/330px-Hsuan_Hua_Hong_Kong_1.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHsuan_Hua_Hong_Kong_1.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Baduanjin_qigong_edit1.jpg/330px-Baduanjin_qigong_edit1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Baduanjin_qigong_edit1.jpg/330px-Baduanjin_qigong_edit1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaduanjin_qigong_edit1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Sree_Narayana_guru_at_Meditation.jpg/500px-Sree_Narayana_guru_at_Meditation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https